CORE broken-cprover-smt-backend
main.c
--no-pointer-check
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ tautology: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ unconstrained value: FAILURE$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
^warning: ignoring
^Invariant check failed
--
Dereferencing a pointer to a struct that has no byte layout, because a member
of non-constant size is followed by further members, must not use the byte
memory model, which cannot represent such a struct. The dereference yields an
unconstrained value instead.
